This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the Administrative Professional (Employee Group) Please note: This is a fixed-term contract position that is set to conclude in January 2030.   
 About the Role:  
 The Transfer Academic Advisor is responsible for providing real-time academic advising through a variety of informative and targeted services to the undergraduate student population, specifically to students who are considering a transfer or who have recently transferred to Brock University from another Ontario university or college. The position provides support and develops educational programming for transfer students in understanding University rules, program and graduation requirements, program options and academic and non-academic services and supports for transfer students across campus. As the primary point of contact for transfer students during the admissions, transfer credit evaluation, course planning, course registration and campus arrival phases, the Transfer Academic Advisor facilitates a seamless academic transition from prospective to current student. The position is also responsible for collecting quantitative and qualitative data pertaining to transfer student interactions, for reporting purposes.  
 The Transfer Academic Advisor will:   
 Provide one-on-one academic advising to prospective transfer students regarding educational pathways between postsecondary institutions and Brock University (i.e. program/course requirements, admission eligibility requirements, academic background requirements, available articulation agreements, etc.);   
 Support students through the transition between an Ontario postsecondary institution and Brock University; assist students with transition plan/steps, when/how to register for courses, academic program plan development (in conjunction with the student’s major advisor), transfer credits, advanced standing, understanding academic regulations and university policies, how to navigate between institutions, and respond to all other student inquiries regarding transition phase;     
 Mentor and monitor the progress of all transfer students and redirect students to a variety of additional support services available on campus where appropriate;  
 Create, attend and present information at outreach group advising sessions specifically designed and delivered to transfer students;  
 Attend recruitment events including Fall Preview Day, Spring Open House, Orientation Sessions and Outreach initiatives, to promote transitional programs to prospective students;  
 Collaborate with campus partners to identify new and/or enhanced transfer student programming opportunities;  
 Conduct market research surveys to better understand transfer student needs and enhance the transfer experience;  
 Develop a heightened presence for transfer support services on campus through the creation of promotional materials and web content;  
 Monitor and report statistics relative to predefined objectives to assess outcomes, determine gaps, and recognize new opportunities to enhance pre-existing programming.  
 Collect data and submit reports regarding transfer student service appointments, walk-ins, and enrolments.   
 Key Skills and Experience:  
 Undergraduate degree in a related field or the equivalent combination of education and experience;  
 Experience with academic and/or student success counselling, in a post-secondary environment;  
 Knowledge of academic advising, including advising models, theories, and techniques, and counselling theories;  
 Understanding of the differences and similarities between university and college practices, policies, protocols and governance structures;  
 Understanding of the Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act (FIPPA);  
 Experience working with computer software and systems including MS Office, internet search engines, web applications, social media platforms, and registration systems;  
 Strong verbal, written, listening, and interpersonal communication skills;  
 Solid presentation and public-speaking skills;  
 Ability to work independently under minimal supervision, as well as part of a team, to identify and conceptualize enhanced transfer student programming opportunities;   
 Promotes and embodies inclusivity and respect within the workplace and the broader community;  
 Sound judgement, resourceful, and ability to address inquiries with confidence and accuracy;  
 Excellent record keeping abilities;  
 Excellent attention to detail with strong research and analytical skills;  
 Excellent organizational skills, with the ability to prioritize to meet deadlines.  
 Preferred or Asset Skills:   
 Post-secondary transfer-related experience preferred   
